      "summary": "W3-GW-I slice 4 (Claude Opus 5.5, R-4). This slice covers section 6 of the design and R-70 (a).\n- New code HB-GRD-005: a run is live, so the gateway refuses judge calls before any spawn (review A1).\n- backend.run_roots and backend.refuse_if_live: the scan covers every worktree's runs/ plus --runs. status.require_known filters out folders that are not runs; a run with liveness alive or stalled refuses the pass. judge_pass runs the check before its first spawn, and the pass's known_roots widen to the same set.\n- The in-run pass uses judge.IN_RUN: every judged metric is NA \"judge calls not allowed in this pass\", with no lookup and no verdict_uses row.\n- bench grade without the flag reads the verdict store only and prints \"judge misses: <n> call(s)\".\n- bench grade --allow-model-calls runs the refusal first and then judge.calling. It reads the operator's e-mail from BENCH_OPERATOR_EMAIL. runner.run_pass gains a \"judging\" parameter.\n- The Copilot branch:\n  - copilot_argv(exe, model) ends in -p. copilot_request prepends JUDGE_SYSTEM on stdin, and invocation_sha256 hashes that stdin template.\n  - A Copilot call copies nothing into an empty COPILOT_HOME. The answer is the record's last assistant.message (copilot_answer).\n  - A tools_advertised value other than [] fails the call with HB-GW-006.\n  - HEADLESS_HARNESSES gains copilot. The probe and its self-test use the builders.\n- Mutants: gateway.json +14 and judge.json +12. mutate_check killed all 81 in gateway.json and all 40 in judge.json.\n- Full pytest: 1542 passed. The 1 failure also fails on main: test_the_committed_freeze_record... (B1 was added to the freeze in 00d6bde). ruff is clean.",
