      "prompt": "Goal: CI-OPT slice 5, the Test Architect's approved Rank 2a (docs/notes/ci-opt-proposal.md, section \"Test Architect review\"; read it first): a pre-turn digest cache inside src/harness_bench/grade/_changes.py so that grading many cells of one task does not re-hash the same pre-turn tree, keyed by content, never by path; red first.\nMeasured (cProfile in the proposal, section 1): _changes.change_set takes about 5.0 s of a 10.5 s grader test, almost all of it _digest over ~1,062 files across the pre-turn and working trees; the pre-turn half is identical for every D1 cell of one task version.\nDone when: change_set (read it and its callers first) caches the pre-turn side's {relpath: digest} map in a process-scoped, bounded cache (e.g. functools.lru_cache or a small dict with a size cap you state) keyed by (the pre-turn commit's tree object id from `git rev-parse <commit>^{tree}` run through the existing gitsafe helper, the digest algorithm tag, and the BUILD_OUTPUT set), never by a filesystem path; when the tree id cannot be read, it does not cache (falls back to computing); tests red first in the grader's test file or a new tests/test_changes_cache.py: (a) differential: on fixtures with CRLF, a UTF-8 BOM, a symlink and a binary file, change_set with the cache equals change_set without it (a way to bypass the cache for the test, e.g. a parameter or clearing it, not a monkeypatch of the digest function); (b) isolation: two pre-turn trees with different tree ids never share an entry (a changed file in the second is seen), and the same tree id at a different path does share it; tests/mutations (the file that covers _changes.py) gains named mutants \"the tree id dropped from the key\" and \"the cache used when the tree id is unreadable\", each killed by (b); the three profiled grader tests' times before and after (uv run pytest --durations=0 on them) go in the commit message; check_regrade's EA==EB stays the runtime proof, nothing else changes; uv run pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_grade_*.py tests/test_check_regrade.py passes; uv run pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider --collect-only exits 0; uv run ruff check src tests tools is clean; A test earns its place by a failure only it catches; Commit each red and each green immediately.\nNot in scope: the working-tree side of change_set; tree_digest in tests (Rank 2b, a later slice); any other grader; ci.yml; any file under runs/; any push.\nTier: T1\nFan-out cap: 0\nContext ceiling: 150k tokens\nMain-line budget: one slice of at most 50 minutes; commit each red and each green immediately.\n\nGrounding: docs/notes/ci-opt-proposal.md (sections 1 and the Test Architect review); src/harness_bench/grade/_changes.py (change_set, _files, _digest, BUILD_OUTPUT, pre_turn_tree); src/harness_bench/gitsafe.py; tests/mutations/*.json (find the file covering _changes.py); tests/test_grade_correctness.py (d1_cell for fixtures). Use python, not python3 (Windows).",
