      "prompt": "Goal: make the driver's cancel-timing tests in tests/test_driver.py deterministic under uv run pytest -n auto, by triggering the cancel on an observed state of the fake agent instead of a wall-clock threading.Timer.\nMeasured (Leader, 2026-09-28, main adb2a92): the R1 worker saw tests/test_driver.py::test_cancel_sends_session_cancel_during_the_prompt fail under -n auto and pass 5 of 5 alone, and a different cancel-timing test failed the same way on a repeat run; the test sets cancel with threading.Timer(0.4, cancel.set) (tests/test_driver.py:179), so a slow spawn under CPU contention can put the cancel before the prompt is sent, which is the handshake path the next test (:196, Timer(0.2)) covers; the timers at :167, :179, :196, :213 and :585 are the sweep set; the fake agent writes .fake-prompt.txt when it receives the prompt (the handshake test asserts its absence).\nDone when: each cancel-timing test in the sweep set whose intended phase depends on the timer firing inside it (during the prompt, during the handshake, or after a hang starts) sets its cancel or terminate when the fake agent has observably reached that phase (for example by polling for the file the fake writes on receiving the prompt, with a bounded wait that fails the test by name if the phase is never reached), or the Leader-visible reason it cannot is written as an assume: beside it; a test that needs the cancel before a phase (the handshake test) holds the fake in that phase (for example the existing handshake_delay) rather than racing it; the fix is proven by a red that is observable: run the prompt-phase test under a forced delay (for example a spawn slowed by a monkeypatched sleep or handshake_delay larger than the old timer) and show it fails on the old code with the stop reason assertion, then passes on the new code; the change names the class in docs/lessons/defect-classes.md (search it for an existing timer-race class and add this as an instance there if one exists, else add the class with the phase-triggered wait as its control); a test earns its place by a failure only it catches, so add no new test beyond the forced-delay proof; uv run pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n auto tests/test_driver.py passes three times in a row; uv run pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n auto passes; uv run ruff check src tests tools is clean; Commit each red and each green immediately.\nNot in scope: src/harness_bench/driver.py behaviour changes; other test files; any file under runs/; any push.\nTier: T1\nFan-out cap: 0\nContext ceiling: 100k tokens\nMain-line budget: one slice of at most 20 minutes; commit each red and each green immediately.\n\nGrounding: tests/test_driver.py (the _spawn helper, the fake agent it launches and the tests at :160-:220 and :580-:600); src/harness_bench/driver.py (run_turn's cancel handling); docs/lessons/defect-classes.md. Use python, not python3 (Windows).",
