      "kind": "prompt",
      "outcome": "success",
      "prompt": "Goal: make the report's Context growth section read a real per-call producer, the model_calls fact, instead of turn_usage, which carries no per-turn grain, so the chart shows measured data for the harnesses whose record is per call; red first.\nMeasured (Leader, 2026-09-28, main 0278c6e): R6b shipped src/harness_bench/report/context_growth.py, whose build(view) reads turn_usage and so renders every task as `No turns recorded for <task>.` under an assume:, because turn_usage is one summed row per (run, cell, attempt, model) (engine.py _usage_per_model); the design's section 4 names turn_usage as ContextGrowth's source, and that is wrong; the model_calls fact holds one row per model call keyed (run_id, extraction_id, principal, native_session_id, native_ordinal, model) (src/harness_bench/views.py:53-55), views reads a cell's rows for its current extraction (views.py ~:474, into Extraction.model_calls via views.model_call), and grade/cost.py `_context_growth` (~:155) already derives a per-call context size from those rows (uncached_input + cache_read + cache_write) with two NA rules, acp_turn (ACP_MISSES_CALLS) and Copilot (SESSION_TOTALS), because those records are not per call; html.render() has run_dir and passes a context_growth_obj seam that tests use.\nDone when: context_growth.build derives, per (combo, pack, task), the per-call context size series from the cell's current-extraction model_calls rows ordered by native_ordinal, keeps only the agent's own calls (principal, cited from its producer; judge or gateway calls excluded), takes the median over repetitions per call index with the min and max band, and marks a compaction where a call's context size drops below the previous call's (an inline assume: states that rule, what would confirm it, and what breaks if it is wrong); a cell whose usage source is acp_turn, or whose harness is copilot, reads NA with the grader's own reason constants imported from grade/cost.py (one definition), never a second copy of the text; the module's old turn_usage assume: is deleted, and docs/design/phase4-report.md section 4's ContextGrowth row names model_calls (and the two NA rules) as its source in the same change; a test that builds a graded fixture run whose model_calls rows grow over three calls and asserts the rendered series equals those rows' sizes in ordinal order is committed red first, failing on an assertion, then green; a test that a Copilot cell reads the SESSION_TOTALS reason is added only if no existing test covers that branch; a named mutant for the ordinal ordering and one for the compaction rule in tests/mutations/report.json, each killed; uv run python tools/mutate_check.py tests/mutations/report.json reads every mutation killed (the Leader runs --touched at the join); uv run pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n auto passes; uv run ruff check src tests tools is clean (run it before each commit); a test earns its place by a failure only it catches; Commit each red and each green immediately.\nNot in scope: the heatmap, the other charts and the summaries section (R7 is in flight in another tree and adds the summaries section to report/html.py: edit only context_growth.py, _context_growth and its helpers, and render()'s one context-growth line if it must change); engine.py and any ledger fact (no new fact: this is derived at report time); board.py; any dependency; any file under runs/; any push.\nTier: T1\nFan-out cap: 0\nContext ceiling: 120k tokens\nMain-line budget: one slice of at most 40 minutes; commit each red and each green immediately.\n\nGrounding: src/harness_bench/report/context_growth.py; src/harness_bench/report/html.py (_context_growth, render); src/harness_bench/views.py (FACTS, KEYS, rows, model_call, the per-cell extraction read near :474); src/harness_bench/grade/cost.py (_context_growth, ACP_MISSES_CALLS, SESSION_TOTALS); src/harness_bench/grade/runner.py (where model_calls rows are appended, and their principal); docs/design/phase4-report.md sections 4 and 6 row 8; tests/test_report.py (the R6b context growth tests); tests/archived_runs.py (fixture builders). Use python, not python3 (Windows). Work only inside the worktree C:/Projects/x-harness-x-model-bench-w4-cg (use absolute paths or cd into it in each shell command).",
