      "summary": "Stopped before authoring: B3 (\"SpecBench task\", scenario 2) cannot be built as its inventory row and task.yaml stub specify.\n\nVerified facts (all cited, no guessing):\n1. Publication is real: arXiv:2605.30314, \"SpecBench: Evaluating Specification-Level Reasoning for Software Engineering LLM Agents\" (Hamblin, Song, Zhu, Jayarajan, Liu, Vijaykumar, Pekhimenko; U. Toronto / U. Waterloo / Vector Institute / NVIDIA), submitted 28 May 2026, cs.MA. Matches the proposal's own citation (docs/proposals/cross-harness-benchmarking-proposal.md line 99/119).\n2. Repository claim in the paper text (\"We open source the benchmark at https://github.com/kevins981/SpecBench\") does not resolve: WebFetch on that URL returns HTTP 404; `gh api repos/kevins981/SpecBench` returns 404 \"Not Found\"; the account kevins981 is real (67 public repos enumerated via `gh api users/kevins981/repos`) but none is named SpecBench in any casing; GitHub code search for \"SpecBench in:name\" returns 16 unrelated repos (different papers/projects), none under kevins981; web.archive.org has never crawled the URL (archived_snapshots: {}); no matching Hugging Face dataset found under the paper's authors. Conclusion: no public repository is currently reachable for this benchmark.\n3. Even setting the missing repo aside, the paper's own described evaluation is not a deterministic, runnable checker: task = given an RFC proposal + codebase + prior RFC history, predict specification deficiencies; scoring = predictions matched against a golden set via a two-stage LLM process (structured Subject-Predicate-Impact decomposition, then an ensemble of two LLM judges [GPT-5.4 and Sonnet 4.6], majority over 4 trials). This requires calling specific paid judge models, which conflicts with this task's binding constraints (never set or ask for an API key; portable, offline oracle; oracle invokes its tool directly with no external model dependency).\n4. Scope mismatch beyond the missing checker: this early version of SpecBench (explicitly labelled \"This early version focuses on identifying specification deficiencies... A future version of SpecBench will evaluate agents' ability to address the deficiencies through specification revision\") does not do \"primer -> spec\" generation, the scenario-2 shape B1/B2 establish. It is a deficiency-critique task against an existing proposal, not a spec-authoring task with a spec_input given.\n\nPer the brief's own stop condition (\"If no public SpecBench with a runnable checker exists, stop and report what you found. Do not invent a benchmark\") and Not in scope (\"If the inventory row cannot be met as written ... stop and report it rather than redefining the task\"), no task.yaml/prompt.md/workspace/tests/oracle content was authored. tasks/B3/task.yaml is left unchanged at status: stub. No commit was made beyond this audit entry.\n\nRecommendation for the Leader: either (a) mark B3 blocked/deferred until SpecBench publishes its repo, (b) substitute a different public benchmark row for B3, or (c) accept an authored (non-\"public checker\") task modelled on SpecBench's method but graded by this repo's own judge grader, which would be a redefinition outside this worker's scope.",
